  "curriculum": "Sections 6.5–6.8 of the 2026–2027 guide give eight first-year units of 7.5 EC, eight second-year units of 7 EC plus 1, 2 and 1 EC skills units, and a third year of 30 EC minor, 20 EC advanced electives and 10 EC thesis with course. The nominal full-time Philosophy degree is Dutch-taught, with English advanced electives available. It is distinct from Philosophy of a Specific Discipline. The guide treats its elective areas as disciplinary groupings rather than formal routes.",
  "progression": "The first year provides history and foundational philosophical subdisciplines. Completion of the first year precedes the normal second-year advanced work, the minor and the selected Year 3 electives. The 30 EC autumn minor may be a permitted minor outside Philosophy, two 15 EC minors, an approved self-designed package or eligible study abroad. Thesis writing requires the completed first and second years, and the accompanying course and thesis count once. The published normal plan reserves 15 EC electives in period 3 and 5 EC in period 4. Applying source order within those slots, choose Heidegger, Democratic Theory and Complicity in period 3, and Medieval and Early Modern Metaphysics in period 4. This avoids putting three electives into the same autumn as the minor, and preserves the order rule independently of UCR fit.",
